-- Topology: the runtime side of a topology app (build step 3 of the
-- distributed-deploys plan, specs/plans/2026-09-21-distributed-authority-and-deploys-plan.md,
-- sections 4.1, 4.2 and II.3 / II.6 "Placement at runtime").
--
-- In a topology app `main` is generated (`march --topology`,
-- lib/desugar/desugar_topology.ml). It starts the ClusterNode, runs each
-- pool's hook under `hook` (a watchdog: a hook must return promptly), and
-- hands this module one `Role` per served role. From then on the NODE owns
-- its offers (D16): `place` opens the offers the topology places on it and
-- re-evaluates on every membership change; `drain_on_signal` closes them on
-- SIGTERM/SIGINT and lets running sessions finish; `supervise_offers` re-offers a
-- role whose offer (or hosting actor) died, and keeps `main` alive.
--
-- Placement rules (4.2), evaluated by every node for itself, with no control
-- plane:
--   everywhere()        offered on every node that serves the role (D18);
--   on_label(label)     offered when this node's labels (MARCH_NODE_LABELS, a
--                   comma-separated list set by the launcher) include it;
--   count(n)            offered on n of the eligible live nodes, chosen by
--                   rendezvous hashing: every node ranks the candidates by
--                   hash(role, node_id) and offers when it is in the top n (D19);
--   count_on(l, n)      count(n) among the nodes carrying label l.
-- "Eligible" for a Count role means: a live member (or this node) that serves
-- the role and carries its label. Other nodes' pools and labels are not in
-- the membership table, so each eligible node registers a cluster name,
-- `topo:<role>/<node_id>`, and the ranking reads those names back; a dead
-- node's names become invisible with its membership. A node that REJOINS
-- counts only after MARCH_PLACEMENT_SETTLE_MS (default 15000), so a flapping
-- node does not pull a role back and forth (hysteresis). `count(1)` is not a
-- lock: during a partition each side may offer, as with any global name.
--
-- The hash is SHA-256 (Crypto.sha256), not the plan's BLAKE3: the runtime's
-- BLAKE3 is not exposed to March code, and the placement only needs a hash
-- that every node computes identically.
--
-- Losing a role is a drain, not a cut: `SessionNode.close_offer` refuses new
-- invitations and lets the sessions already running finish.
--
-- Re-reading the topology (D16, build step 8). `place` installs a SIGHUP
-- watcher: on SIGHUP the node re-reads MARCH_TOPOLOGY_FILE (the digest,
-- `.forge/topology.json`, which the reconciler rewrites before signalling)
-- and applies what changed for the roles its build contains: a new
-- placement, a role this process's pools no longer serve (its offer is
-- closed: a drain), a new capacity (the offer is closed and reopened at the
-- new size). The next evaluation opens and closes offers as for a
-- membership change; nothing restarts. A role newly served that this build
-- has no code for is reported, not offered: that needs a rebuild. The node
-- reports what it applied and the offers it holds to MARCH_TOPOLOGY_STATUS
-- (`forge topology status` reads it). The reconciler never opens or closes
-- an offer itself.
mod Topology do
  needs IO
  needs IO.Mut
  needs IO.Spawn
  needs IO.Clock
  needs IO.Signal
  needs IO.Process
  needs IO.Console
  needs IO.NetConnect
  needs IO.NetListen
  needs IO.FileRead
  needs IO.FileWrite
  needs Session.Live
  needs ClusterNode.Live

  -- ── placement rules and roles ─────────────────────────────────────────

  -- Constructor names are prefixed: a bare `Count` collided with DataFrame's
  -- nullary `Count` aggregate in user code that writes it unqualified. Type
  -- names are prefixed too (`TopoPlacement`, `TopoRole`, ...): March has one
  -- global type namespace, and a bare `Placement` broke a user program that
  -- declares its own (test/session/cluster_placement).
  -- `PlaceNowhere`: not served by this process's pools (after a reload
  -- moved the role to another pool).
  type TopoPlacement = PlaceEverywhere | PlaceOn(String) | PlaceCount(Int) | PlaceCountOn(String, Int) | PlaceNowhere

  doc "Offer the role on every node that serves it (no `place` in the topology)."
  fn everywhere() : TopoPlacement do PlaceEverywhere end
  doc "Offer the role on the nodes whose MARCH_NODE_LABELS include [label] (`place = { on = label }`)."
  fn on_label(label : String) : TopoPlacement do PlaceOn(label) end
  doc "Offer the role on [n] of the eligible live nodes, by rendezvous hashing (`place = { count = n }`)."
  fn count(n : Int) : TopoPlacement do PlaceCount(n) end
  doc "`count(n)` among the nodes carrying [label] (`place = { on = label, count = n }`)."
  fn count_on(label : String, n : Int) : TopoPlacement do PlaceCountOn(label, n) end

  -- What an open offer needs to be supervised: the offer, and whether
  -- whatever serves its sessions is still alive (a hosted role's actor; a
  -- function role has nothing beyond the offer itself).
  -- [capacity]: the size it was opened at (0: fixed by the build). [stop]:
  -- what ends whatever served it once its closed offer has drained (a hosted
  -- role's actor exits then, 6.1; a function role has nothing to stop).
  type TopoOpened = { ap : SessionNode.Offer, alive : Int -> Bool, capacity : Int, stop : Int -> () }

  -- One served role: its "Protocol.Role" name, its placement, its capacity,
  -- and how to open one offer of it on this node at a capacity. The
  -- generated `main` builds these with `offer_role` and `offer_actor_role`
  -- (capacity from the topology, changeable by a reload); `role` and
  -- `actor_role` fix the capacity in the code they are given (capacity 0,
  -- the argument `open` receives is ignored).
  type TopoRole = { name : String, place : TopoPlacement, capacity : Int,
                open : Int -> Result(TopoOpened, SessionNode.RunError) }

  doc """
  A role bound to a function (`body = "M.f"` in `[roles]`). [open] is the
  generated `<P>_Run.offer_<R>(io, node, capacity, fn (s, caps..., st) ->
  M.f(env, s, caps..., st))`.
  """
  fn role(name : String, place : TopoPlacement, open : () -> Result(SessionNode.Offer, SessionNode.RunError)) : TopoRole do
    { name: name, place: place, capacity: 0,
      open: fn _ ->
        match open() do
          Ok(o) -> Ok({ ap: o, alive: fn _ -> true, capacity: 0, stop: fn _ -> () })
          Err(e) -> Err(e)
        end }
  end

  doc """
  A role bound to a function, offered at [capacity] sessions: [open] is the
  generated `fn topology_cap -> <P>_Run.offer_<R>(io, node, topology_cap,
  ...)`. A reload that changes the role's capacity reopens its offer at the
  new size.
  """
  fn offer_role(name : String, place : TopoPlacement, capacity : Int,
                open : Int -> Result(SessionNode.Offer, SessionNode.RunError)) : TopoRole do
    { name: name, place: place, capacity: capacity,
      open: fn cap ->
        match open(cap) do
          Ok(o) -> Ok({ ap: o, alive: fn _ -> true, capacity: cap, stop: fn _ -> () })
          Err(e) -> Err(e)
        end }
  end

  doc """
  A role bound to an actor (`actor = "M.A"` in `[roles]`, D23): one actor per
  offer, spawned by [mk] (the generated `fn () -> spawn(M.A, env)`) and handed
  to [open] (the generated `<P>_Run.offer_hosted_<R>` call whose start,
  deliver and cancel callbacks forward to it). An actor spawned for an offer
  that could not be opened is kept for the next attempt rather than spawned
  again. Supervision re-offers the role when its actor dies. When the offer
  closes (placement moved the role, its capacity changed, or its protocol
  did: `reoffer`), the actor keeps serving the sessions it hosts and is
  stopped once they have all ended (6.1: a protocol change spawns a new
  hosting actor; the old one drains and exits).
  """
  fn actor_role(name : String, place : TopoPlacement, mk : () -> Pid(a),
                open : Pid(a) -> Result(SessionNode.Offer, SessionNode.RunError)) : TopoRole do
    offer_actor_role(name, place, 0, mk, fn (a, _) -> open(a))
  end

  doc """
  `actor_role`, offered at [capacity] sessions: [open] takes the actor and
  the capacity (the generated `fn (topology_a, topology_cap) ->
  <P>_Run.offer_hosted_<R>(io, node, topology_cap, topology_a, ...)`).
  """
  fn offer_actor_role(name : String, place : TopoPlacement, capacity : Int, mk : () -> Pid(a),
                      open : Pid(a) -> Int -> Result(SessionNode.Offer, SessionNode.RunError)) : TopoRole do
    let spare = Vault.new("topology_spare_" ++ name ++ "_" ++ int_to_string(next_id()))
    { name: name, place: place, capacity: capacity,
      open: fn cap ->
        let host = match Vault.get(spare, "h") do
          Some(h) -> h
          None -> mk()
        end
        match open(host, cap) do
          Ok(o) ->
            Vault.drop(spare, "h")
            Ok({ ap: o, alive: fn _ -> is_alive(host), capacity: cap, stop: fn _ -> kill(host) })
          Err(e) ->
            Vault.set(spare, "h", host)
            Err(e)
        end }
  end

  pfn next_id() : Int do
    let ids : Vault(Int) = Vault.open("topology_ids")
    Vault.incr(ids, "n", 1)
  end

  -- ── the pure core: who offers what ────────────────────────────────────

  doc "Labels from a comma-separated list: `\"db, public\"` is `[\"db\", \"public\"]`."
  fn labels_of(s : String) : List(String) do
    List.filter(List.map(String.split(s, ","), String.trim), fn l -> not(String.is_empty(l)))
  end

  doc "This node's labels: MARCH_NODE_LABELS, comma-separated (set by the launcher from the overlay)."
  fn node_labels() : List(String) do labels_of(Env.get("MARCH_NODE_LABELS", "")) end

  doc "A node's rendezvous score for [role]: every node computes the same one."
  fn score(role_name : String, node_id : String) : String do
    Crypto.sha256(role_name ++ "\n" ++ node_id)
  end

  doc "[ids] ranked for [role_name], best first (highest score; ties by id)."
  fn rank(role_name : String, ids : List(String)) : List(String) do
    let scored = List.map(List.dedup(ids), fn id -> (score(role_name, id), id))
    let sorted = List.sort_by(scored, fn (a, b) ->
      match (a, b) do
        ((sa, ia), (sb, ib)) -> if sa == sb do ia < ib else sa > sb end
      end)
    List.map(sorted, fn p -> match p do (_, id) -> id end)
  end

  doc "Whether this node may take part in [p] at all: it carries the label, if any."
  fn eligible_here(p : TopoPlacement, labels : List(String)) : Bool do
    match p do
      PlaceEverywhere -> true
      PlaceOn(l) -> List.member(labels, l)
      PlaceCount(_) -> true
      PlaceCountOn(l, _) -> List.member(labels, l)
      PlaceNowhere -> false
    end
  end

  doc "Whether [p] ranks nodes (and so needs the eligible set)."
  fn ranked(p : TopoPlacement) : Bool do
    match p do
      PlaceCount(_) -> true
      PlaceCountOn(_, _) -> true
      _ -> false
    end
  end

  doc """
  Whether node [me], with [labels], offers [role_name] under [p], given the
  settled eligible nodes [eligible] (other nodes; [me] is added when it is
  eligible itself).
  """
  fn wants(p : TopoPlacement, role_name : String, me : String, labels : List(String), eligible : List(String)) : Bool do
    if not(eligible_here(p, labels)) do false
    else
      match p do
        PlaceCount(n) -> List.member(List.take(rank(role_name, Cons(me, eligible)), n), me)
        PlaceCountOn(_, n) -> List.member(List.take(rank(role_name, Cons(me, eligible)), n), me)
        _ -> true
      end
    end
  end

  doc "A member that rejoined at [rejoined_at] counts again once [settle_ms] have passed."
  fn settled(now : Int, rejoined_at : Option(Int), settle_ms : Int) : Bool do
    match rejoined_at do
      None -> true
      Some(t) -> now - t >= settle_ms
    end
  end

  doc "The name an eligible node registers for a ranked role."
  fn marker(role_name : String, node_id : String) : String do
    "topo:" ++ role_name ++ "/" ++ node_id
  end

  -- The node ids behind every marker of [role_name] in [names].
  fn marked(role_name : String, names : List(String)) : List(String) do
    let prefix = "topo:" ++ role_name ++ "/"
    let k = String.byte_size(prefix)
    List.filter_map(names, fn nm ->
      if String.starts_with(nm, prefix) do Some(String.slice(nm, k, String.byte_size(nm) - k)) else None end)
  end

  pfn settle_ms() : Int do Env.get_int("MARCH_PLACEMENT_SETTLE_MS", 15000) end
  pfn tick_ms() : Int do Env.get_int("MARCH_PLACEMENT_TICK_MS", 200) end
  pfn hook_timeout_ms() : Int do Env.get_int("MARCH_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS", 10000) end

  -- ── per-node state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  -- The process a node's placement markers are bound to.
  -- A field name no other stdlib or user record is likely to share: a
  -- declared record type is found by its SHAPE in places (the `@[remote]`
  -- codec choice), and `{ n : Int }` made a user's `type Hit = { n : Int }`
  -- ambiguous.
  type TopoAnchorState = { topology_anchor_marks : Int }

  actor Anchor do
    state { topology_anchor_marks : Int }
    init  { topology_anchor_marks: 0 }
    on Nop() do state end
    -- The placement loop, restarted from here after a deploy (build step 9):
    -- a task runs the code of the epoch it was spawned in, and this actor has
    -- passed its marker, so the loop it spawns runs the new code -- opening
    -- a changed protocol's offer under its new fingerprint.
    on Respawn(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), st : TopoState) do
      let _ = task_spawn(fn _ -> do
        reoffer_with(node, st)
        place_loop(node, st)
      end)
      state
    end
  end

  -- Everything `place`, `drain_on_signal` and `supervise_offers` share,
  -- found by the node's id so the three need only the node.
  type TopoState = { meta : Vault(Int), strs : Vault(String), offers : Vault(TopoOpened), draining : Vault(TopoOpened),
                 roles : Vault(List(TopoRole)), anchor : Vault(Pid(TopoAnchorState)) }

  pfn state_of(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live)) : TopoState do
    let k = ClusterNode.node_id(node)
    { meta: Vault.open("topology_meta_" ++ k), strs: Vault.open("topology_strs_" ++ k),
      offers: Vault.open("topology_offers_" ++ k),
      draining: Vault.open("topology_draining_" ++ k), roles: Vault.open("topology_roles_" ++ k),
      anchor: Vault.open("topology_anchor_" ++ k) }
  end

  pfn anchor(st : TopoState) : Pid(TopoAnchorState) do
    match Vault.get(st.anchor, "a") do
      Some(a) -> a
      None ->
        let a = spawn(Anchor)
        Vault.set(st.anchor, "a", a)
        a
    end
  end

  -- Reports go to stdout, prefixed: `print_stderr` exists in both backends
  -- but not in the typechecker's builtin table.
  -- The node's name for messages: its own membership entry, else its id.
  pfn label(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live)) : String do
    let me = ClusterNode.node_id(node)
    match List.find(ClusterNode.all_members(node), fn m -> m.node_id == me) do
      Some(m) -> m.name
      None -> me
    end
  end

  pfn report(msg : String) : () do println("topology: " ++ msg) end

  -- ── placement ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  doc """
  Open the offers the topology places on [node], one per entry of [roles],
  and keep them placed: a task re-evaluates every MARCH_PLACEMENT_TICK_MS
  (default 200 ms) against the current membership, opening a role this node
  now ranks for and closing (draining) one it no longer does. Membership
  events are recorded as they arrive; a node that rejoins counts after the
  settling period. Returns once the first evaluation has opened its offers.
  """
  fn place(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), roles : List(TopoRole)) : () do
    let st = state_of(node)
    Vault.set(st.roles, "roles", roles)
    Vault.set(st.roles, "base", roles)
    Signal.watch(Signal.Hup, fn -> reload(node))
    let meta = st.meta
    let _ = ClusterNode.subscribe(node, fn ev ->
      match ev do
        ClusterNode.NodeRejoined(i) -> Vault.set(meta, "r:" ++ i.node_id, unix_time_ms())
        _ -> ()
      end)
    reconcile(node, st)
    write_status(node, st)
    let _ = task_spawn(fn _ -> place_loop(node, st))
    ()
  end

  pfn place_loop(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), st : TopoState) : Int do
    sleep_ms(tick_ms())
    if Vault.get(st.meta, "closing") != None do 0
    else if Vault.get(st.meta, "stopped") != None do 0
    -- A deploy made this loop's epoch old: hand over to a loop on the new
    -- code (the anchor's, which has moved past its marker) and end.
    else if epoch_draining() do
      let _ = send(anchor(st), Respawn(node, st))
      0
    else
      reconcile(node, st)
      write_status(node, st)
      place_loop(node, st)
    end end end
  end

  -- The other nodes eligible for [r], settled, as this node sees them.
  pfn eligible_others(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), st : TopoState, r : TopoRole, now : Int) : List(String) do
    -- A suspect member still counts: a role moves only once SWIM declares
    -- its node Dead (4.2), not on every missed probe.
    let alive = List.filter_map(ClusterNode.all_members(node), fn m ->
      match m.status do
        Membership.Dead -> None
        _ -> Some(m.node_id)
      end)
    let settle = settle_ms()
    List.filter(marked(r.name, ClusterNode.names(node)), fn id ->
      id != ClusterNode.node_id(node) && List.member(alive, id) && settled(now, Vault.get(st.meta, "r:" ++ id), settle))
  end

  doc """
  Re-evaluate [node]'s placement now, as the next tick would. For tests that
  drive membership through a fake dictionary and should not wait for a tick
  (run them with a long MARCH_PLACEMENT_TICK_MS).
  """
  fn reconcile_now(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live)) : () do reconcile(node, state_of(node)) end

  pfn reconcile(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), st : TopoState) : () do
    let labels = node_labels()
    let now = unix_time_ms()
    let roles = Vault.get_or(st.roles, "roles", Nil)
    List.each(roles, fn r -> reconcile_role(node, st, labels, now, r))
    watch_draining(st, now)
  end

  pfn reconcile_role(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), st : TopoState, labels : List(String), now : Int, r : TopoRole) : () do
    let here = eligible_here(r.place, labels)
    if ranked(r.place) do mark(node, st, r.name, here) else () end
    let others = if ranked(r.place) do eligible_others(node, st, r, now) else Nil end
    let want = wants(r.place, r.name, ClusterNode.node_id(node), labels, others)
    match Vault.get(st.offers, r.name) do
      None ->
        if want do open_role(st, r) else () end
      Some(o) ->
        if not(want) do
          report(r.name ++ ": no longer placed on " ++ label(node) ++ "; draining its offer")
          retire(st, r.name, o)
        else if r.capacity > 0 && o.capacity != r.capacity do
          report(r.name ++ ": capacity " ++ int_to_string(o.capacity) ++ " -> " ++ int_to_string(r.capacity)
                 ++ "; draining its offer and opening one at the new size")
          retire(st, r.name, o)
        else if Vault.get(st.meta, "supervise") != None && not(healthy(o)) do
          report(r.name ++ ": its offer or hosting actor died; offering it again")
          retire(st, r.name, o)
        else () end end end
    end
  end

  -- Register (or release) this node's marker for a ranked role.
  pfn mark(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), st : TopoState, role_name : String, here : Bool) : () do
    let name = marker(role_name, ClusterNode.node_id(node))
    let held = ClusterNode.lookup(node, name) != None
    if here && not(held) do
      let _ = ClusterNode.register(node, name, anchor(st))
      ()
    else if not(here) && held do ClusterNode.unregister(node, name)
    else () end end
  end

  pfn open_role(st : TopoState, r : TopoRole) : () do
    match (r.open)(r.capacity) do
      Ok(o) ->
        Vault.drop(st.meta, "e:" ++ r.name)
        Vault.set(st.offers, r.name, o)
      -- The previous offer's name is released asynchronously: try again on
      -- the next tick without reporting it.
      Err(SessionNode.AlreadyOffered(_)) -> ()
      Err(e) ->
        -- Report a failure once, not every tick.
        if Vault.get(st.meta, "e:" ++ r.name) == None do
          Vault.set(st.meta, "e:" ++ r.name, 1)
          report(r.name ++ ": could not offer: " ++ SessionNode.run_error_message(e))
        else () end
    end
  end

  doc """
  Re-open each of [node]'s open offers with the code now running
  (distributed-deploys build step 9): an offer whose protocol fingerprint
  changed is opened again under the new one (a hosted role with a fresh
  actor) and the old offer is closed; its sessions finish on the old
  version and a hosting actor exits once they have (6.1). An offer whose
  fingerprint did not change stays as it is (the new offer's name is
  already taken). The placement loop runs this itself after a deploy; call
  it directly only from a test.
  """
  fn reoffer(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live)) : () do reoffer_with(node, state_of(node)) end

  pfn reoffer_with(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), st : TopoState) : () do
    let roles = Vault.get_or(st.roles, "roles", Nil)
    List.each(roles, fn r ->
      match Vault.get(st.offers, r.name) do
        None -> ()
        Some(o) ->
          match (r.open)(if o.capacity > 0 do o.capacity else r.capacity end) do
            Ok(fresh) ->
              if fresh.ap.fingerprint == o.ap.fingerprint do
                -- Opened under another name with the same version (should not
                -- happen: the name carries the fingerprint); keep one.
                SessionNode.close_offer(fresh.ap)
                (fresh.stop)(0)
              else
                report(r.name ++ ": protocol changed on " ++ label(node)
                       ++ "; offering the new version and draining the old one")
                retire(st, r.name, o)
                Vault.set(st.offers, r.name, fresh)
              end
            -- Same fingerprint: this version is already offered.
            Err(SessionNode.AlreadyOffered(_)) -> ()
            Err(e) -> report(r.name ++ ": could not offer its new version: " ++ SessionNode.run_error_message(e))
          end
      end)
  end

  -- Close [o] (sessions already running finish) and keep it for the drain.
  pfn retire(st : TopoState, role_name : String, o : TopoOpened) : () do
    SessionNode.close_offer(o.ap)
    Vault.drop(st.offers, role_name)
    let key = role_name ++ "#" ++ int_to_string(next_id())
    Vault.set(st.draining, key, o)
    Vault.set(st.meta, "t:" ++ key, unix_time_ms())
  end

  -- An offer closed while the node keeps running (placement or a reload
  -- moved its role) drains under the topology's deadlines: its sessions are
  -- reported once still running at the soft deadline, and again at the hard
  -- one. They are not cut: cancelling one offer's sessions needs a
  -- SessionNode API that does not exist yet (a process-wide drain on
  -- SIGTERM still ends at `drain_on_signal`'s hard deadline). A drained
  -- offer is forgotten.
  pfn watch_draining(st : TopoState, now : Int) : () do
    let soft = Vault.get_or(st.meta, "drain_soft", 30000)
    let hard = Vault.get_or(st.meta, "drain_hard", 120000)
    List.each(Vault.all(st.draining), fn kv ->
      match kv do
        (key, o) ->
          let n = active(o)
          let since = now - Vault.get_or(st.meta, "t:" ++ key, now)
          if n == 0 do
            -- Drained: whatever served it (a hosting actor) is done.
            (o.stop)(0)
            Vault.drop(st.draining, key)
            Vault.drop(st.meta, "t:" ++ key)
            Vault.drop(st.meta, "w:" ++ key)
          else
            let warned = Vault.get_or(st.meta, "w:" ++ key, 0)
            if since >= hard && warned < 2 do
              Vault.set(st.meta, "w:" ++ key, 2)
              report(key ++ ": hard drain deadline passed with " ++ int_to_string(n) ++ " session(s) still running on its closed offer")
            else if since >= soft && warned < 1 do
              Vault.set(st.meta, "w:" ++ key, 1)
              report(key ++ ": soft drain deadline passed with " ++ int_to_string(n) ++ " session(s) still running on its closed offer")
            else () end end
          end
      end)
  end

  pfn healthy(o : TopoOpened) : Bool do
    is_alive(o.ap.worker) && (o.alive)(0)
  end

  doc "The roles [node] offers right now, by name, sorted."
  fn offered(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live)) : List(String) do
    let st = state_of(node)
    List.sort_by(Vault.keys(st.offers), fn (a, b) -> a < b)
  end

  doc "The actor answering invitations for [role_name]'s open offer on [node], if one is open."
  fn offer_worker(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), role_name : String) : Option(Pid(SessionNode.OfferCount)) do
    let st = state_of(node)
    match Vault.get(st.offers, role_name) do
      Some(o) -> Some(o.ap.worker)
      None -> None
    end
  end

  -- Sessions still running under [o].
  pfn active(o : TopoOpened) : Int do
    match get_actor_field(o.ap.worker, "active") do
      Some(n) -> n
      None -> 0
    end
  end

  doc "Sessions still running on [node]'s offers, open or draining."
  fn running(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live)) : Int do
    let st = state_of(node)
    let sum = fn (acc, kv) -> match kv do (_, o) -> acc + active(o) end
    List.fold_left(Vault.all(st.draining), List.fold_left(Vault.all(st.offers), 0, sum), sum)
  end

  -- ── re-reading the topology (SIGHUP) ──────────────────────────────────

  doc "A placement as the topology writes it, for reports."
  fn placement_text(p : TopoPlacement) : String do
    match p do
      PlaceEverywhere -> "everywhere"
      PlaceOn(l) -> "on " ++ l
      PlaceCount(n) -> "count " ++ int_to_string(n)
      PlaceCountOn(l, n) -> "count " ++ int_to_string(n) ++ " on " ++ l
      PlaceNowhere -> "not served here"
    end
  end

  pfn json_int(j : Option(Json.JsonValue)) : Option(Int) do
    match j do
      Some(Json.Number(f)) -> Some(float_to_int(f))
      _ -> None
    end
  end

  pfn json_str(j : Option(Json.JsonValue)) : Option(String) do
    match j do
      Some(Json.Str(s)) -> Some(s)
      _ -> None
    end
  end

  pfn json_list(j : Option(Json.JsonValue)) : List(Json.JsonValue) do
    match j do
      Some(Json.Array(xs)) -> xs
      _ -> Nil
    end
  end

  doc """
  A digest's `place` object as a placement: null is everywhere (D18),
  `{ on }`, `{ count }`, or both.
  """
  fn placement_of_json(j : Option(Json.JsonValue)) : TopoPlacement do
    match j do
      Some(Json.Object(_)) ->
        let pj = Option.unwrap_or(j, Json.Null)
        match (json_str(Json.get(pj, "on")), json_int(Json.get(pj, "count"))) do
          (Some(l), Some(n)) -> PlaceCountOn(l, n)
          (Some(l), None) -> PlaceOn(l)
          (None, Some(n)) -> PlaceCount(n)
          (None, None) -> PlaceEverywhere
        end
      _ -> PlaceEverywhere
    end
  end

  -- A role as the digest describes it: (name, placement, capacity).
  type TopoDesired = { d_name : String, d_place : TopoPlacement, d_capacity : Int }

  doc """
  What the digest [text] asks of this process: for each role one of
  [pools] serves, its placement and capacity (a role no such pool serves is
  absent); the drain deadlines; and an error for text that is not a
  version-1 digest.
  """
  fn desired_of(text : String, pools : String -> Bool) : Result((List(TopoDesired), Int, Int), String) do
    match Json.parse(text) do
      Err(e) -> Err("not JSON: " ++ e)
      Ok(dj) ->
        if json_int(Json.get(dj, "version")) != Some(1) do Err("not a version-1 topology digest")
        else
          let served = List.flat_map(json_list(Json.get(dj, "pools")), fn p ->
            match json_str(Json.get(p, "name")) do
              Some(n) ->
                if pools(n) do
                  List.filter_map(json_list(Json.get(p, "serves")), fn r -> json_str(Some(r)))
                else Nil end
              None -> Nil
            end)
          let roles = List.filter_map(json_list(Json.get(dj, "roles")), fn r ->
            match json_str(Json.get(r, "name")) do
              Some(n) ->
                if List.member(served, n) do
                  Some({ d_name: n, d_place: placement_of_json(Json.get(r, "place")),
                         d_capacity: Option.unwrap_or(json_int(Json.get(r, "capacity")), 64) })
                else None end
              None -> None
            end)
          let drain = Option.unwrap_or(Json.get(dj, "drain"), Json.Null)
          let soft = Option.unwrap_or(json_int(Json.get(drain, "soft_ms")), 30000)
          let hard = Option.unwrap_or(json_int(Json.get(drain, "hard_ms")), 120000)
          Ok((roles, soft, hard))
        end
    end
  end

  doc """
  [base] (the roles this build contains, as the generated `main` placed
  them) under [desired]: a role the digest no longer serves here is
  `PlaceNowhere`; otherwise its placement and (unless fixed by the build,
  capacity 0) its capacity come from the digest.
  """
  fn apply_desired(base : List(TopoRole), desired : List(TopoDesired)) : List(TopoRole) do
    List.map(base, fn r ->
      match List.find(desired, fn d -> d.d_name == r.name) do
        None -> { r with place: PlaceNowhere }
        Some(d) -> { r with place: d.d_place, capacity: if r.capacity == 0 do 0 else d.d_capacity end }
      end)
  end

  pfn find_role(roles : List(TopoRole), name : String) : Option(TopoRole) do
    List.find(roles, fn r -> r.name == name)
  end

  pfn report_change(before : List(TopoRole), r : TopoRole) : () do
    match find_role(before, r.name) do
      Some(b) ->
        if placement_text(b.place) != placement_text(r.place) do
          report(r.name ++ ": placement " ++ placement_text(b.place) ++ " -> " ++ placement_text(r.place))
        else () end
      None -> ()
    end
  end

  pfn report_unbuilt(base : List(TopoRole), d : TopoDesired) : () do
    match find_role(base, d.d_name) do
      Some(_) -> ()
      None -> report(d.d_name ++ ": now served by this node's pool, but this build has no code for it; rebuild and restart to offer it")
    end
  end

  doc """
  Re-read the topology now, as SIGHUP does: MARCH_TOPOLOGY_FILE is parsed
  and the roles this build contains take their placement and capacity from
  it; the next evaluation (run at once) opens and drains offers to match.
  A file that cannot be read or parsed changes nothing and is reported.
  """
  fn reload(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live)) : () do
    let st = state_of(node)
    if Vault.get(st.meta, "closing") != None do () else
      match process_env("MARCH_TOPOLOGY_FILE") do
        None -> report("SIGHUP: MARCH_TOPOLOGY_FILE is not set; there is no topology to re-read")
        Some(path) ->
          match File.read(path) do
            Err(_) -> report("SIGHUP: could not read " ++ path ++ "; placement unchanged")
            Ok(text) ->
              match desired_of(text, fn p -> runs_pool(p)) do
                Err(e) -> report("SIGHUP: " ++ path ++ ": " ++ e ++ "; placement unchanged")
                Ok((desired, soft, hard)) ->
                  let base : List(TopoRole) = Vault.get_or(st.roles, "base", Nil)
                  let before : List(TopoRole) = Vault.get_or(st.roles, "roles", Nil)
                  let after = apply_desired(base, desired)
                  List.each(after, fn r -> report_change(before, r))
                  List.each(desired, fn d -> report_unbuilt(base, d))
                  Vault.set(st.meta, "drain_soft", soft)
                  Vault.set(st.meta, "drain_hard", hard)
                  Vault.set(st.roles, "roles", after)
                  Vault.set(st.strs, "applied", Crypto.sha256(text))
                  report("topology re-read from " ++ path)
                  reconcile(node, st)
                  write_status(node, st)
              end
          end
      end
    end
  end

  -- ── status (for the reconciler) ───────────────────────────────────────

  doc """
  What this node reports to the reconciler: its name, the digest it applied
  (sha256, or `compiled` before any reload), its offers, how many closed
  offers are still draining, and the sessions running on them all.
  """
  fn status_text(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live)) : String do
    let st = state_of(node)
    "node " ++ label(node) ++ "\n"
    ++ "topology " ++ Vault.get_or(st.strs, "applied", "compiled") ++ "\n"
    ++ "offers " ++ String.join(offered(node), ",") ++ "\n"
    ++ "draining " ++ int_to_string(List.length(Vault.keys(st.draining))) ++ "\n"
    ++ "running " ++ int_to_string(running(node)) ++ "\n"
  end

  -- Write the status to MARCH_TOPOLOGY_STATUS when it changed (atomically:
  -- a temporary file renamed over it, so a reader never sees half).
  pfn write_status(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), st : TopoState) : () do
    match process_env("MARCH_TOPOLOGY_STATUS") do
      None -> ()
      Some(path) ->
        let text = status_text(node)
        if Vault.get(st.strs, "status") == Some(text) do () else
          let tmp = path ++ ".tmp"
          match File.write(tmp, text) do
            Ok(_) ->
              let _ = File.rename(tmp, path)
              Vault.set(st.strs, "status", text)
            Err(_) -> ()
          end
        end
    end
  end

  -- ── draining ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  doc """
  Stop placing and close every offer of [node] (running sessions finish):
  what SIGTERM does under `drain_on_signal`. Returns at once.
  """
  fn close_all(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live)) : () do
    let st = state_of(node)
    Vault.set(st.meta, "closing", 1)
    List.each(Vault.all(st.offers), fn kv -> match kv do (name, o) -> retire(st, name, o) end)
  end

  doc """
  On SIGTERM or SIGINT: close every offer of [node] (new invitations are
  refused), drain every code epoch the process runs (running sessions end
  at their next loop boundary, D27, and actors take the epoch drain's
  deadlines), then exit 0 once no session is running. At [soft_ms] a drain
  still waiting is reported; at [hard_ms] the process exits 1, naming how
  many sessions it cut. A second signal escapes the watcher and stops the
  process at once.
  """
  fn drain_on_signal(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), soft_ms : Int, hard_ms : Int) : () do
    Signal.watch(Signal.Term, fn -> drain(node, soft_ms, hard_ms))
    Signal.watch(Signal.Int, fn -> drain(node, soft_ms, hard_ms))
  end

  doc "Drain [node] now, as SIGTERM does under `drain_on_signal`."
  fn drain(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), soft_ms : Int, hard_ms : Int) : () do
    let st = state_of(node)
    if Vault.get(st.meta, "closing") != None do () else
      report("draining " ++ label(node) ++ " (soft " ++ int_to_string(soft_ms) ++ " ms, hard "
             ++ int_to_string(hard_ms) ++ " ms)")
      close_all(node)
      -- The epoch drain (DD step 6, follow-up 5): the same as the reload
      -- server's `DRAIN` for every epoch this process runs. Sessions end at
      -- their next loop boundary (D27); the hard deadline below exits the
      -- process before the epoch drain's own would matter, so only the soft
      -- one is armed here. (The stdlib-only builtin: this function has no
      -- `Cap(IO)` and its signature is the generated main's.)
      epoch_drain(soft_ms, 0)
      let t0 = unix_time_ms()
      let _ = task_spawn(fn _ -> drain_wait(node, soft_ms, hard_ms, t0, false))
      ()
    end
  end

  pfn drain_wait(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live), soft_ms : Int, hard_ms : Int, t0 : Int, warned : Bool) : Int do
    let n = running(node)
    let spent = unix_time_ms() - t0
    if n == 0 do
      report("drained " ++ label(node))
      process_exit(0)
      0
    else if spent >= hard_ms do
      report("hard deadline: stopping " ++ label(node) ++ " with " ++ int_to_string(n) ++ " session(s) still running")
      process_exit(1)
      1
    else
      let w = if not(warned) && spent >= soft_ms do
        report("soft deadline passed with " ++ int_to_string(n) ++ " session(s) still running")
        true
      else warned end
      sleep_ms(50)
      drain_wait(node, soft_ms, hard_ms, t0, w)
    end end
  end

  -- ── supervision ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  doc """
  Re-offer any role whose offer actor, or hosting actor, has died, and keep
  the calling task (the generated `main`) alive until the node stops or
  drains. A process whose `main` returned would exit, taking its offers
  with it.
  """
  fn supervise_offers(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live)) : () do
    let st = state_of(node)
    Vault.set(st.meta, "supervise", 1)
    supervise_wait(st)
  end

  pfn supervise_wait(st : TopoState) : () do
    if Vault.get(st.meta, "stopped") != None do ()
    else
      sleep_ms(250)
      supervise_wait(st)
    end
  end

  doc """
  Stop [node] and everything placed on it: close every offer (running
  sessions are cut when the node goes), end placement and `supervise_offers`,
  then `ClusterNode.stop`. For a program (a test, say) that ends on its own
  rather than on a signal.
  """
  fn stop(node : Cap(ClusterNode.Live)) : () do
    let st = state_of(node)
    close_all(node)
    Vault.set(st.meta, "stopped", 1)
    ClusterNode.stop(node)
  end

  -- ── hooks ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  doc """
  Run the pool hook [name] ([f]), which must return promptly: offers open
  only after every hook has returned. A watchdog reports a hook still
  running after MARCH_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS (default 10000) and exits the process
  with status 1: offering nothing would be worse than failing loudly.
  Long-lived work belongs in a task or actor the hook spawns.
  """
  fn hook(name : String, f : () -> a) : a do
    let flag : Vault(Int) = Vault.new("topology_hook_" ++ int_to_string(next_id()))
    let limit = hook_timeout_ms()
    let _ = task_spawn(fn _ -> watchdog(flag, name, limit, unix_time_ms()))
    let v = f()
    Vault.set(flag, "done", 1)
    v
  end

  pfn watchdog(flag : Vault(Int), name : String, limit : Int, t0 : Int) : Int do
    if Vault.get(flag, "done") != None do 0
    else if unix_time_ms() - t0 >= limit do
      report("hook " ++ name ++ " did not return within " ++ int_to_string(limit)
             ++ " ms (MARCH_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS); a hook must return promptly -- start long-lived work in a task or actor")
      process_exit(1)
      1
    else
      sleep_ms(50)
      watchdog(flag, name, limit, t0)
    end end
  end

  -- ── starting the node ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

  doc """
  The node's configuration from the environment (`ClusterNode.config_from_env`),
  with defaults for a lone local run: MARCH_NODE_NAME defaults to `local-1`
  and MARCH_NODE_PORT to 7946.
  """
  fn config_from_env() : ClusterNode.CnConfig do
    let name = Env.get("MARCH_NODE_NAME", "local-1")
    let port = Env.get_int("MARCH_NODE_PORT", 7946)
    let seeds = labels_of(Env.get("MARCH_CLUSTER_NODES", ""))
    let creation = Env.get_int("MARCH_NODE_CREATION", unix_time_ms())
    ClusterNode.config(name, port, Env.get("MARCH_NODE_ADVERTISE", ""), seeds,
                       Env.get("MARCH_CLUSTER_SECRET", "march-cluster"), creation)
  end

  doc """
  Report that the node could not start ([why]) and stop the program with
  status 1. The generated `main` starts the node itself --
  `ClusterNode.start(io, Topology.config_from_env())` -- because only
  `ClusterNode` may hand out a `Cap(ClusterNode.Live)`.
  """
  fn start_failed(why : String) : a do
    report(why)
    process_exit(1)
    panic(why)
  end

  doc """
  Whether this process runs pool [pool]: MARCH_POOLS (comma-separated) names
  the pools a process of a shared build runs; unset, it runs every pool the
  build contains (`forge run`'s one process, D9).
  """
  fn runs_pool(pool : String) : Bool do
    match process_env("MARCH_POOLS") do
      None -> true
      Some(s) ->
        let ps = labels_of(s)
        List.is_empty(ps) || List.member(ps, pool)
    end
  end
end
